IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc16-search-warrants.l4 -- sections 487 and 487.01 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XV): the search warrant and the general warrant.
-- Part agent ccc16. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the keel's core only.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Conventions: as in ccc16-open-court.l4 (a "may" whose "if"/"satisfied" gate fails answers NOTHING; a "shall"/"must" requirement not met answers JUST FALSE; a "where" gate that fails
-- on a "may" answers JUST FALSE under ruling (b) of 2026-11-05, counted in the fork register). Seams: `s 2 offence-related property` (MAYBE BOOLEAN) and `s 552 judge` (MAYBE BOOLEAN).

§ `Section 487 -- Information for search warrant`

-- 487(1) A justice who is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in a building, receptacle or place (a) anything on or in respect of which any offence ... has been or is
-- suspected to have been committed, (b) anything that ... will afford evidence ..., (c) anything ... intended to be used for the purpose of committing any offence against the person for which a person may be arrested without warrant,
-- or (c.1) any offence-related property, may at any time issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer ... named in the warrant (d) to search ... and to seize it, and (e) ... to bring the thing seized before ... a justice.
-- src:9014 | 487 (1) A justice who is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in a building, receptacle or place
-- src:9015 | (a) anything on or in respect of which any offence against this Act or any other Act of Parliament has been or is suspected to have been committed,
-- src:9016 | (b) anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe will afford evidence with respect to the commission of an offence, or will reveal the whereabouts of a person who is believed to have committed an offence, against this Act or any other Act of Parliament,
-- src:9017 | (c) anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe is intended to be used for the purpose of committing any offence against the person for which a person may be arrested without warrant, or
-- src:9018 | (c.1) any offence-related property,
-- src:9019 | may at any time issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament and who is named in the warrant
-- src:9020 | (d) to search the building, receptacle or place for any such thing and to seize it, and
-- src:9021 | (e) subject to any other Act of Parliament, to, as soon as practicable, bring the thing seized before, or make a report in respect of it to, a justice in accordance with section 489.1.
@ref s 487(1) (the grounds) (src:9014-9021)
GIVEN `the justice is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place anything on or in respect of which any offence against this Act or any other Act of Parliament has been or is suspected to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe will afford evidence with respect to the commission of an offence, or will reveal the whereabouts of a person who is believed to have committed an offence, against this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe is intended to be used for the purpose of committing any offence against the person for which a person may be arrested without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 offence-related property: there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place any offence-related property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(1) the justice may issue a warrant to search the building, receptacle or place` MEANS
    IF    `the justice is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1`
      AND (   `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place anything on or in respect of which any offence against this Act or any other Act of Parliament has been or is suspected to have been committed`
           OR `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe will afford evidence with respect to the commission of an offence, or will reveal the whereabouts of a person who is believed to have committed an offence, against this Act or any other Act of Parliament`
           OR `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe is intended to be used for the purpose of committing any offence against the person for which a person may be arrested without warrant`
           OR (`s 2 offence-related property: there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in the building, receptacle or place any offence-related property` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice who is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in a building, receptacle or place"

-- src:9019 | may at any time issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament and who is named in the warrant
@ref s 487(1) (who may be named) (src:9019)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is named in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(1) the warrant may authorize the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is named in the warrant` AND (`the person is a peace officer` OR `the person is a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "authorizing a peace officer or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament and who is named in the warrant"

DECLARE `s 487(1) what the warrant authorizes` IS ONE OF
    `s 487(1)(d) to search the building, receptacle or place for any such thing and to seize it`
    `s 487(1)(e) subject to any other Act of Parliament, to, as soon as practicable, bring the thing seized before, or make a report in respect of it to, a justice in accordance with section 489.1`
    `s 487(1) something else`

-- src:9019 | may at any time issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament and who is named in the warrant
-- src:9020 | (d) to search the building, receptacle or place for any such thing and to seize it, and
-- src:9021 | (e) subject to any other Act of Parliament, to, as soon as practicable, bring the thing seized before, or make a report in respect of it to, a justice in accordance with section 489.1.
@ref s 487(1)(d), (e) (src:9019-9021)
GIVEN act IS A `s 487(1) what the warrant authorizes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(1) the warrant may authorize the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 487(1) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) to search the building, receptacle or place for any such thing and to seize it, and (e)"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487(2) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
-- src:9023 | (2) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref s 487(2) (the place) (src:9023)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(2) the warrant may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be executed at any place in Canada"

-- src:9023 | (2) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref s 487(2) (the officer's authority) (src:9023)
GIVEN `the officer is a public officer named in the warrant or a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(2) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the officer is a public officer named in the warrant or a peace officer`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant"
    ELSE IF `the officer has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed"

-- 487(2.1) A person authorized under this section to search a computer system in a building or place for data may (a) use or cause to be used any computer system ... to search any data ...; (b) reproduce ... any data in the form of a print-out or other intelligible output;
-- (c) seize the print-out or other output for examination or copying; and (d) use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data.
DECLARE `s 487(2.1) what the person may do` IS ONE OF
    `s 487(2.1)(a) use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place to search any data contained in or available to the computer system`
    `s 487(2.1)(b) reproduce or cause to be reproduced any data in the form of a print-out or other intelligible output`
    `s 487(2.1)(c) seize the print-out or other output for examination or copying`
    `s 487(2.1)(d) use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data`
    `s 487(2.1) something else`

-- src:9025 | (2.1) A person authorized under this section to search a computer system in a building or place for data may
-- src:9026 | (a) use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place to search any data contained in or available to the computer system;
-- src:9027 | (b) reproduce or cause to be reproduced any data in the form of a print-out or other intelligible output;
-- src:9028 | (c) seize the print-out or other output for examination or copying; and
-- src:9029 | (d) use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data.
@ref s 487(2.1)(a) to (d) (src:9025-9029)
GIVEN `the person is authorized under section 487 to search a computer system in a building or place for data` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 487(2.1) what the person may do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(2.1) the person may do the act` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is authorized under section 487 to search a computer system in a building or place for data`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person authorized under this section to search a computer system in a building or place for data may"
    ELSE CONSIDER act
         WHEN `s 487(2.1) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may (a) use or cause to be used any computer system"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487(2.2) Every person who is in possession or control of any building or place in respect of which a search is carried out under this section shall, on presentation of the warrant, permit the person carrying out the search (a) to use ... any computer
-- system ... to search any data ... for data that the person is authorized by this section to search for; (b) to obtain a hard copy of the data and to seize it; and (c) to use ... any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data.
DECLARE `s 487(2.2) what the person in possession or control must permit` IS ONE OF
    `s 487(2.2)(a) to use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place in order to search any data contained in or available to the computer system for data that the person is authorized by this section to search for`
    `s 487(2.2)(b) to obtain a hard copy of the data and to seize it`
    `s 487(2.2)(c) to use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data`
    `s 487(2.2) something else`

-- src:9030 | Duty of person in possession or control
-- src:9031 | (2.2) Every person who is in possession or control of any building or place in respect of which a search is carried out under this section shall, on presentation of the warrant, permit the person carrying out the search
-- src:9032 | (a) to use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place in order to search any data contained in or available to the computer system for data that the person is authorized by this section to search for;
-- src:9033 | (b) to obtain a hard copy of the data and to seize it; and
-- src:9034 | (c) to use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data.
@ref s 487(2.2)(a) to (c) (src:9030-9034)
GIVEN `the person is in possession or control of a building or place in respect of which a search is carried out under section 487` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant has been presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 487(2.2) what the person in possession or control must permit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(2.2) the person in possession or control must permit the person carrying out the search to do the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is in possession or control of a building or place in respect of which a search is carried out under section 487`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who is in possession or control of any building or place in respect of which a search is carried out under this section"
        IF (act EQUALS `s 487(2.2) something else`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "permit the person carrying out the search (a) to use or cause to be used any computer system"
        IF (NOT `the warrant has been presented`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on presentation of the warrant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487(3) A search warrant issued under this section may be in the form set out as Form 5 in Part XXVIII, varied to suit the case. (Form 5 only prescribes the wording of a document: machinery; the permission as to form is encoded.)
-- src:9035 | Form
-- src:9036 | (3) A search warrant issued under this section may be in the form set out as Form 5 in Part XXVIII, varied to suit the case.
@ref s 487(3) (src:9035-9036)
GIVEN `the warrant is in the form set out as Form 5 in Part XXVIII, varied to suit the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(3) the search warrant may be in the form set out as Form 5` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is in the form set out as Form 5 in Part XXVIII, varied to suit the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be in the form set out as Form 5 in Part XXVIII, varied to suit the case"

§ `Section 487.01 -- Information for general warrant`

-- 487.01(1) A provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 may issue a warrant in writing authorizing a peace officer to, subject to this section, use any device or investigative technique or
-- procedure or do any thing described in the warrant that would, if not authorized, constitute an unreasonable search or seizure in respect of a person or a person's property if (a) ... reasonable grounds to believe that an offence ... has been or will be committed
-- and that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the use of the technique, procedure or device or the doing of the thing; (b) ... in the best interests of the administration of justice; and (c) there is no other provision ... that would provide for a warrant.
-- src:9039 | 487.01 (1) A provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 may issue a warrant in writing authorizing a peace officer to, subject to this section, use any device or investigative technique or procedure or do any thing described in the warrant that would, if not authorized, constitute an unreasonable search or seizure in respect of a person or a person’s property if
-- src:9040 | (a) the judge is satisfied by information on oath in writing that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed and that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the use of the technique, procedure or device or the doing of the thing;
-- src:9041 | (b) the judge is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant; and
-- src:9042 | (c) there is no other provision in this or any other Act of Parliament that would provide for a warrant, authorization or order permitting the technique, procedure or device to be used or the thing to be done.
@ref s 487.01(1) (src:9039-9042)
GIVEN `the person is a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 552 judge: the person is a judge as defined in section 552` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath in writing that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed and that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the use of the technique, procedure or device or the doing of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no other provision in this or any other Act of Parliament that would provide for a warrant, authorization or order permitting the technique, procedure or device to be used or the thing to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(1) the judge may issue a warrant in writing authorizing a peace officer to use the device, technique or procedure or do the thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is a provincial court judge` OR `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` OR (`s 552 judge: the person is a judge as defined in section 552` EQUALS JUST TRUE))) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 may issue a warrant in writing"
        IF `the judge is satisfied by information on oath in writing that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed and that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the use of the technique, procedure or device or the doing of the thing` AND `the judge is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant` AND `there is no other provision in this or any other Act of Parliament that would provide for a warrant, authorization or order permitting the technique, procedure or device to be used or the thing to be done` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that would, if not authorized, constitute an unreasonable search or seizure in respect of a person or a person’s property if"

-- 487.01(2) Nothing in subsection (1) shall be construed as to permit interference with the bodily integrity of any person.
-- src:9043 | Limitation
-- src:9044 | (2) Nothing in subsection (1) shall be construed as to permit interference with the bodily integrity of any person.
@ref s 487.01(2) (src:9043-9044)
GIVEN `the act is an interference with the bodily integrity of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(2) subsection (1) permits the act` MEANS
    IF `the act is an interference with the bodily integrity of a person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (1) shall be construed as to permit interference with the bodily integrity of any person"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of interference with bodily integrity

-- 487.01(3) A warrant issued under subsection (1) shall contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances.
-- src:9045 | Search or seizure to be reasonable
-- src:9046 | (3) A warrant issued under subsection (1) shall contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 487.01(3) (src:9045-9046)
GIVEN `the warrant is issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant contains such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(3) the warrant contains the terms and conditions required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the warrant is issued under subsection (1)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant issued under subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF `the warrant contains such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable"

-- 487.01(4) A warrant issued under subsection (1) that authorizes a peace officer to observe, by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device, any person who is engaged in activity in circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation
-- of privacy shall contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that the privacy of the person or of any other person is respected as much as possible.
-- src:9047 | Video surveillance
-- src:9048 | (4) A warrant issued under subsection (1) that authorizes a peace officer to observe, by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device, any person who is engaged in activity in circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy shall contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that the privacy of the person or of any other person is respected as much as possible.
@ref s 487.01(4) (src:9047-9048)
GIVEN `the warrant authorizes a peace officer to observe, by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device, any person who is engaged in activity in circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant contains such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that the privacy of the person or of any other person is respected as much as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(4) the warrant contains the privacy terms and conditions required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the warrant authorizes a peace officer to observe, by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device, any person who is engaged in activity in circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that authorizes a peace officer to observe, by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device, any person who is engaged in activity in circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy"
    ELSE IF `the warrant contains such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that the privacy of the person or of any other person is respected as much as possible`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable to ensure that the privacy of the person or of any other person is respected as much as possible"

-- 487.01(5) The definition offence in section 183 and sections 183.1, 184.2, 184.3 and 185 to 188.2, subsection 189(5), and sections 190, 193 and 194 to 196 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a warrant referred to in subsection (4).
-- Section numbers are decimals, so "185 to 188.2" and "194 to 196" are range tests (185, 186.1, 188.2 are inside; 189 and 188.3 are outside).
-- src:9049 | Other provisions to apply
-- src:9050 | (5) The definition offence in section 183 and sections 183.1, 184.2, 184.3 and 185 to 188.2, subsection 189(5), and sections 190, 193 and 194 to 196 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a warrant referred to in subsection (4) as though references in those provisions to interceptions of private communications were read as references to observations by peace officers by means of television cameras or similar electronic devices of activities in circumstances in which persons had reasonable expectations of privacy.
@ref s 487.01(5) (src:9049-9050)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the warrant is a warrant referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(5) the provision applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the warrant` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the warrant is a warrant referred to in subsection (4)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a warrant referred to in subsection (4)"
    ELSE IF    `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 183 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 183.1 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 184.2 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 184.3
            OR (`the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 185 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 188.2)
            OR (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 189 AND `the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(5)")
            OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 190 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 193
            OR (`the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 194 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 196)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists the provisions that apply and does not say that no other applies

-- 487.01(5.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) that authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly shall require, as part of the terms and conditions referred to in subsection (3), that notice of the entry and search be given
-- within any time after the execution of the warrant that the judge considers reasonable in the circumstances.
-- src:9051 | Notice after covert entry
-- src:9052 | (5.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) that authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly shall require, as part of the terms and conditions referred to in subsection (3), that notice of the entry and search be given within any time after the execution of the warrant that the judge considers reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 487.01(5.1) (src:9051-9052)
GIVEN `the warrant authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant requires that notice of the entry and search be given within the time after the execution of the warrant that the judge considers reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(5.1) the warrant requires notice of the covert entry and search as required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the warrant authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly"
    ELSE IF `the warrant requires that notice of the entry and search be given within the time after the execution of the warrant that the judge considers reasonable in the circumstances`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall require, as part of the terms and conditions referred to in subsection (3), that notice of the entry and search be given"

-- 487.01(5.2) Where the judge who issues a warrant under subsection (1) or any other judge having jurisdiction to issue such a warrant is, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of an application to vary the period within which the notice referred to in
-- subsection (5.1) is to be given, satisfied that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge may grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, but no extension may exceed three years.
-- "no extension may exceed three years": at most three years (the core's Length of time: "three years less a day" is under three years).
-- src:9053 | Extension of period for giving notice
-- src:9054 | (5.2) Where the judge who issues a warrant under subsection (1) or any other judge having jurisdiction to issue such a warrant is, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of an application to vary the period within which the notice referred to in subsection (5.1) is to be given, is satisfied that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge may grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, but no extension may exceed three years.
@ref s 487.01(5.2) (the cap) (src:9053-9054)
GIVEN extension IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(5.2) the extension does not exceed three years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (extension's years TIMES 12 PLUS extension's months) LESS THAN 36 THEN TRUE
        IF (extension's years TIMES 12 PLUS extension's months) EQUALS 36 THEN ((extension's days EQUALS 0) OR extension's `less a day`)
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:9053 | Extension of period for giving notice
-- src:9054 | (5.2) Where the judge who issues a warrant under subsection (1) or any other judge having jurisdiction to issue such a warrant is, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of an application to vary the period within which the notice referred to in subsection (5.1) is to be given, is satisfied that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge may grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, but no extension may exceed three years.
@ref s 487.01(5.2) (src:9053-9054)
GIVEN `the judge is the judge who issued the warrant or another judge having jurisdiction to issue such a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to vary the period is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      extension IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(5.2) the judge may grant an extension of the period for giving notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the judge is the judge who issued the warrant or another judge having jurisdiction to issue such a warrant` AND `the application to vary the period is supported by an affidavit` AND `the judge is satisfied that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application`)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the judge who issues a warrant under subsection (1) or any other judge having jurisdiction to issue such a warrant is, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of an application to vary the period"
        IF (NOT (`s 487.01(5.2) the extension does not exceed three years` extension)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but no extension may exceed three years"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487.01(6) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
-- src:9055 | Execution in Canada
-- src:9056 | (6) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref s 487.01(6) (the place) (src:9055-9056)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(6) the general warrant may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be executed at any place in Canada"

-- src:9055 | Execution in Canada
-- src:9056 | (6) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref s 487.01(6) (the officer's authority) (src:9055-9056)
GIVEN `the officer is a peace officer who executes the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01(6) the peace officer who executes the general warrant has the authority required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the officer is a peace officer who executes the warrant`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any peace officer who executes the warrant"
    ELSE IF `the officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed"
